  "title": "SynOE-OD: Synthetic Outlier-Exposure-based Object Detection",
  "summary": "SynOE-OD is a synthetic outlier-exposure-based object detection method that leverages text-guided inpainting and an open-vocabulary object detector to generate and verify synthetic outliers offline, enabling the fine-tuning of a detector with an added OOD class. This method outperforms existing open-vocabulary baselines on the OoDIS benchmark, achieving AP_50:95, 29.4%, and 39.2% on RoadObstacle, RoadAnomaly, and Fishyscapes datasets.",
